336 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 289 0 R
/E (What do young audiences want from franchises? The box office data gives us one potential answer: diverse representation. Adolescents today are more racially diverse than any prior generation, more likely to identify as LGBTQ+, and more likely to have grown up alongside peers from different backgrounds, and it shows. According to the UCLA Hollywood Diversity Report, films with more diverse casts make more money: for instance, films with casts that were between 40% and 50% people of color \(the U.S. population is 45.2% people of color\) made more than double their budgets on average, while films with casts that were at least 90% White lost money on average. This pattern of success for more diverse casts has been consistent across years of data for domestic and global box office earnings. Yet studios have been wary of backing these projects with higher budgets: diverse representation in film is often concentrated in lower-budget, non-franchise films. The breakdown of 2024 films by the lead's identity illustrates this pattern: )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [13 619 0 R 15 620 0 R 17 621 0 R 19]
>>
endobj
