/E (Diverse representation tends to perform well overseas! Despite a common misconception to the contrary, CSS research has shown that around three-quarters \(75%\) of international audiences want to see films about cultures other than their own. Work from USC Annenberg has shown that films with both leads who are people of color and more racial diversity overall tend to make more money in overseas markets than films with less racial diversity or White leads. )
/Pg 18 0 R
