2018 0 obj
<<
/Title (For example, the Black Panther franchise is a superhero franchise, but it incorporates elements of African culture and Afrofuturist ideas with enormous care. The franchise is very intentional about including nuggets of African culture throughout the films, from the traditional stacked neck rings in the wardrobe to the use of the South African language Xhosa in dialogue. Instead of the culture being a trait of the character, it is integrated into the world itself. In our data, experts rated Black Panther somewhat highly, but young audiences rated it very highly - the third highest rated franchise overall. The cultural elements resonate with young audiences, and unsurprisingly, the franchise has been incredibly successful. For more info on cultural representation, see the roadmap to AIR.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2013 0 R
/Next 2025 0 R
>>
endobj
2019 0 obj
<<
/Title (Minimal roles for characters Adolescents also associated franchises that gave minimal roles to characters with the relevant identity with poor representation. For example, if the character has a minimal impact on the plot, gets sparse characterization, lacks any story arc, or simply does not get to speak or be seen on screen much, they probably have a minimal role, and for adolescents that can really undermine a portrayal of a diverse character. In our data, this is best exemplified by LGBTQ representation, as we explore below.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2013 0 R
/Prev 2025 0 R
>>
