/Title (Context Corner: The Queerness of Minor Roles  Looking at the top 100 grossing films from 2024, USC Annenberg's Inequality in 1,800 Popular Films Report found that only 18 of the 100 films included LGBTQ+ characters. But even this overstates the prominence of LGBTQ+ roles. Among those 100 films, less than 1% of characters with speaking roles were LGBTQ+. This is especially troubling in light of the recent Trevor Project finding that seeing LGBTQ representation in TV/film is the number one thing that makes LGBTQ+ youth feel good about their identity.)
